Write a Java program to find the sum of all elements in a Circular Singly Linked List.

Program:

import java.util.*;


class Main {
    static class Node {
        int data;
        Node next;


        Node(int data) {
            this.data = data;
        }
    }


    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);


        int n = sc.nextInt();
        Node head = null, tail = null;


        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            Node newNode = new Node(sc.nextInt());


            if (head == null) {
                head = tail = newNode;
                tail.next = head;
            } else {
                tail.next = newNode;
                tail = newNode;
                tail.next = head;
            }
        }


        int sum = 0;
        Node temp = head;


        do {
            sum += temp.data;
            temp = temp.next;
        } while (temp != head);


        System.out.println("Sum = " + sum);
    }
}

Input:

5
10 20 30 40 50

Output:

Sum = 150



